  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 505,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 544,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70805,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 182,
        "headingId": 544,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Epididymal cystadenoma is usually located in the caput epididymis {16841375}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:42:09"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 506,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 545,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70806,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 182,
        "headingId": 545,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The symptoms include scrotal mass and infertility, and 10% of patients present with pain. Bilaterality has been reported {1225459}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:42:09"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 507,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 546,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70807,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 182,
        "headingId": 546,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Insufficient data</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:42:09"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 508,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 547,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70808,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 182,
        "headingId": 547,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:42:09"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 509,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 548,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70809,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 182,
        "headingId": 548,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Epididymal cystadenoma is derived from a proliferation of the epithelium of the efferent ductular system located in the caput epididymis {16841375}. Epididymal cystadenoma may also represent a hamartomatous lesion of ectatic efferent ducts {7756240}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:42:09"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 516,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 555,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70810,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 182,
        "headingId": 555,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The cyst surface is smooth. On the cut section, the cyst may be unilocular or multilocular and is often filled with clear fluid {16040296}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:42:09"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 510,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 549,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70811,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 182,
        "headingId": 549,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tubular and cystic structures are lined by a single row of bland tall columnar cells with eosinophilic cytoplasm. Although these may also be papillary, they lack the cuboidal, clear cell morphology of the papillary cystadenoma. No mitosis, necrosis, or pleomorphism is observed {16841375}.</p>\r\n<p>The differential diagnosis includes metastases from prostatic carcinoma in the paratesticular region. The cystadenoma may show microcystic, cribriform, and microglandular areas; however, the cells lack nuclear atypia and prominent nucleoli. The cells are negative for PSA and PAP {16040296; 6612245}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:42:09"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 511,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 550,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70812,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 182,
        "headingId": 550,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:42:09"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 512,
